$y={(\\frac{1}{9})}^{x}+c.$ Determine the value of $c$ and find the equation of the curve." :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote of $y={(\\frac{1}{9})}^{x}$ is $y=0.$\n\nThe vertical translation $y={(\\frac{1}{9})}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=2.5.$ Therefore, $c=2.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "617f0fe6-7998-5d77-b11f-55a0eca11440" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Vertically Shifted and Stretched Exponential Decay Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11991a9d-264d-57e7-9fdd-da7348694651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/77/77ddeefbcbd24c80f6ed0bb7a29d2a43e3151436b0a60b56686b1c67ca31c738.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390540} {:answer/id #uuid "f32fd0b0-49ce-539d-9672-8d020e261fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f73be44a90c4a240b316bcf7ac5586b54ed1ca4cdedfac42f055cd39086ffe2d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390541} {:answer/id #uuid "407fad6c-67c3-5a63-bb5b-a49d0b7c8b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f4/f405cfe76e1d69d7ecad35e96ced1c76c1b64130a118d881d331bcb0b119068c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390542} {:answer/id #uuid "a9519e6c-79f2-5f62-a983-2670eb2a7aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/33f78e0590a7039f0e2e17d5bc871e0503dd3526d282b5fb76e4ef0f3b78cc28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390543} {:answer/id #uuid "29d4d4e8-fe84-544d-8606-3bfce7839133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9d332fa8d3d8ef65daaf34bf906c5ca7cd7e2edaf562386ed4e0ebc4555b0a64.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29d4d4